  "chatter": "<p>Ohio has two competitive top-of-the-ticket contests, as well as several competitive House<span class=\"widont\">&nbsp;</span>races.</p>\n<p>For the U.S. Senate, incumbent Republican Jon Husted, who was appointed to fill Vice President Vance’s seat, faces a tough challenge from Sherrod Brown, who’s trying to get back to the Senate. The race has drawn lots of money, and is considered a toss<span class=\"widont\">&nbsp;</span>up.</p>\n<p>And for the open governor’s contest, Democrat Amy Acton, a former state health official, faces entrepreneur and Trump ally Vivek Ramaswamy. A <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/21/nx-s1-6010530/vivek-ramaswamys-attack-ad-features-mother-of-amy-acton-who-alleges-childhood-abuse\" target=\"_blank\">controversial ad</a> by the Republican Ramaswamy has affected the race’s final<span class=\"widont\">&nbsp;</span>days.</p>\n"
